{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b88ef43e-fef9-4a0c-be7d-41660d57468e","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Start with a right triangle. The side opposite the right angle is the hypotenuse, c.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Squares on a right triangle"},{"op":"figure","id":"squares","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4.7,7.7],"y":[-3.7,7.7],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"vertex_a","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"vertex_b","at":[3,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"vertex_c","at":[0,4]},{"kind":"segment","id":"leg_a","from":{"at":"vertex_a"},"to":{"at":"vertex_b"},"label":"a = 3"},{"kind":"segment","id":"leg_b","from":{"at":"vertex_c"},"to":{"at":"vertex_a"},"label":"b = 4"},{"kind":"segment","id":"hypotenuse","from":{"at":"vertex_b"},"to":{"at":"vertex_c"},"label":"c = 5"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"vertex_a"},"from":{"at":"vertex_b"},"to":{"at":"vertex_c"},"label":"90°"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b88ef43e-fef9-4a0c-be7d-41660d57468e","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Build a square outward on each short side. Their areas are three squared and four squared: nine and sixteen.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"leg_squares","on":"squares","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"square_a","points":[{"at":"vertex_a"},[0,-3],[3,-3],{"at":"vertex_b"}],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","id":"square_b","points":[{"at":"vertex_a"},{"at":"vertex_c"},[-4,4],[-4,0]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"text","at":[1.5,-1.6],"text":"a² = 9"},{"kind":"text","at":[-2,2],"text":"b² = 16"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"small_areas","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"a^2=3^2=9,\\qquad b^2=4^2=16"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b88ef43e-fef9-4a0c-be7d-41660d57468e","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The hypotenuse square has area twenty-five, exactly nine plus sixteen. For every right triangle, the two smaller square areas sum to the largest.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"hyp_square","on":"squares","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"square_c","points":[{"at":"vertex_b"},[7,3],[4,7],{"at":"vertex_c"}],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"text","at":[3.5,3.5],"text":"c² = 25"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"area_sum","anchor":{"el":"small_areas","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"9+16=25"},{"op":"equation","id":"theorem","anchor":{"el":"area_sum","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\boxed{a^2+b^2=c^2}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which side must c represent in the Pythagorean theorem?","expected_gist":"The hypotenuse, opposite the right angle."}}}
